\par Axen returned to his quarters and slumped wearily into the bunk.  He looked around the room, sparse and undecorated.  The place felt as empty as his soul.  }{\i\f5\cf4 All this work, all this fighting, and what have I got to show for it?
\par }{\f5\cf4 
\par He knew the answer even as he posed the question.  His work was his life, for better or worse.  He had to see this thing through, and then... what?
\par 
\par Never mind that.  He couldn't see the end of the current situation, though there had to be one, in death or in triumph.  It was just that right now, he felt very, very tired.
\par 
\par He thought about zoning out watching the EnterCom, but decided to check his mail first.  The first item caught his immediate attention.  It was from the Council, a quarters reassignment.  He read the text carefully, then read it again.
\par 
\par Then he stood up so quickly he nearly bashed his head on the cupboard over the bunk.  "They can't do this!"  All thought of rest was gone; he had work to do.  They'd taken Kraft, kept him out of the loop, but nothing they'd done so far compared to this.  
He was being exiled, and he wasn't going to stand still for it.
\par 
\par }\pard \qc\li360\ri360\nowidctlpar {\f5\cf4 # # #
